59,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option A seems the safest! Transport is cheap, and we won't have to worry about those scary non-refundable deposits for a whole building. It's the fairest way to make sure no one gets stuck with extra costs!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"While Option A is safe, I worry it may not encourage the bonding we need. Option C, with its own building and shared meals, seems like a lovely way for everyone to truly connect.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option B is out of the question; the municipal reservation system is a bureaucratic nightmare. Option C is better, as the owner handles meals, removing the cooking burden from the organizers.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Option B sounds like a nightmare! Eight people to a room? No way! Option C sounds like a real adventure, and since the owner does the meals, we can actually relax! I vote for C!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option C is too risky. The transport costs for two prefectures would be enormous, and the whole-building let means we'd be liable for non-refundable deposits. Option A is the only fiscally responsible choice.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"I see your point, Misaki! Option C is way too risky with the money. Even if it sounds like an adventure, I can't support something where a few people might end up paying for others!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"I understand the financial risks, but I worry that Option A is too similar to our daily routine. If we stay on campus, will the members who feel distant truly find a way to bond?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Bonding is irrelevant if the organizers are burnt out. Option A is convenient, but Option C eliminates the cooking duty and the lottery stress of Option B. Between A and C, C is the more sustainable choice for the staff.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,"But Option A is just school! Where's the fun in that? If we want to actually feel like we're on a camp, we have to go somewhere new. Option C is the only one that's exciting!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Misaki,,Excitement doesn't pay the bills. Option C's distance and booking terms are a recipe for another deficit. Option A ensures we stay within budget and avoids the risk of non-refundable losses.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,"I really want it to be fun, but I can't ignore the risk! If we go with C and someone cancels, it'll be a disaster for our wallets. I'm voting for Option A to keep it fair!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"It is a difficult choice. However, knowing that some members have stopped attending, I feel we must prioritize a place that fosters true connection. I will vote for Option C to bring us all together.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,Option A is too close to our daily routine and doesn't solve the issue of catering if we use campus facilities. Option C is the only choice that ensures the organizers aren't burdened with cooking. I vote for C.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Rin,,"I'm with Ryuji and Shizue! Option A is boring, and Option B is a sleep-deprivation trap. Let's go to the coast for a real adventure where we can actually sleep and eat! Option C!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"I cannot support Option C. The combination of high transport costs and non-refundable deposits is a financial gamble the club cannot afford. To ensure we don't face another deficit, I vote for Option A.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm sorry, everyone, but I have to stick with Option A! I want us all to have fun, but not at the cost of someone's wallet. Let's keep it fair and safe! Option A!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"I hope you can all understand my heart on this. For the sake of our club's future and the happiness of every member, I believe the Coastal Lodge is the right choice. Option C.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"The logic is clear. Option B is a bureaucratic disaster and Option A doesn't solve the labor issue. To protect the organizers from burnout and ensure a functional camp, we must choose Option C. I vote for C.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Rin,,"I'm sticking with my guns! Option A is just more school, and Option B is a no-go. Let's go for the adventure and the good sleep! My final vote is Option C!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Misaki,,My priority is the club's financial stability. Option C is far too risky given the transport costs and deposit terms. I cannot allow another deficit. My final vote is Option A.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
